      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/assets/44f3144d089201597af3ffe32176741b15cbb2345c635549058148f83781175a.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡E=$",
      "worked_solution": "The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H). Relative to the angle $E,$ the adjacent side is $\\overset{―}{FE},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overset{―}{DE}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡E & =\\frac{FE}{DE}=\\frac{80}{89}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
