    "q-54095": {
      "dom_id": "step-q54095",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/assets/14c05d01cdba24b04330a821597eef21dd325228bb8a7fc1e02103ca80f39450.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{cos}⁡S=$",
      "worked_solution": "The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H). Relative to the angle $S,$ the adjacent side is $\\overset{―}{ST},$ and the hypotenuse is $\\overset{―}{SR}.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡S & =\\frac{ST}{SR} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{\\sqrt{19}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{133}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
