    "q-121889": {
      "dom_id": "step-q121889",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/assets/d08a4d0946265ba1314831913b7c31de68fb59845fca42b2b79707c04dbd827c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{8},$ the value of $x$ is",
      "worked_solution": "The cosine of an angle is equal to the adjacent divided by the hypotenuse (C-A-H).\n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta ,$ the length of the adjacent side is $\\frac{7}{4}x+29,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is $7x+17.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{8} & =\\frac{(\\frac{7}{4}x+29)}{7x+17} \\\\ 5(7x+17) & =8(\\frac{7}{4}x+29) \\\\ 35x+85 & =14x+232 \\\\ 21x & =147 \\\\ x & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
